ellent","good","brilliant","best","brilliant","best","best","best","best","good","best","mistake","great","best","best","best","inaccuracy","best","best","mistake","inaccuracy","good","excellent","good","excellent","best","excellent","good","excellent","best","best","best","best","excellent","good","inaccuracy","good","mistake","best","best","best","best","inaccuracy","best","best","best","great","best","best","best","great","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","good","best","best","good","best","best","good","best","excellent","best","best","excellent","excellent","best","excellent","excellent","best","excellent","excellent","mistake","miss","excellent","excellent","mistake","miss","best","best","mistake","miss","inaccuracy","best","best","excellent","best","best","best","excellent","best","excellent","best","excellent","best","excellent","best","excellent","best","good","best","best","best","best","forced","best","best","excellent","forced","best"],"moments":[{"ply":13,"name":"7.Bxc6+","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"7.Bxc6+! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Takes the knight on c6.","Protects the queen on d4, which was hanging.","The next best move, 7.Qa4, would drop White's winning chances from 51% to 31% (−2.23).","7.Bxc6+ trades bishop for knight and protects the queen on d4.","Trades bishop for knight.","Gives check, so the reply is forced."]},{"ply":39,"name":"20.b3","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"20.b3! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Makes an escape square for the king, so back-rank checks lose their sting.","The next best move, 20.Bf4, would drop White's winning chances from 56% to 18% (−4.15).","20.b3 stops the mate threat …Qxb2#.","Black was threatening …Qxb2#, with mate in 1. b3 takes care of it.","Black answers 20…Qc5, opening the line of the rook on b8 to the b3 pawn.","Engine line: 20…Qc5 21.Kb1 Rb4 22.Re3 h5 23.Bc1 (+0.45)."]},{"ply":43,"name":"22.Rxd5","cls":"brilliant","color":"w","headline":"22.Rxd5!! A real sacrifice: White gives up material and the engine still rates it best.","points":["Puts the rook on d5 where it can be taken.","Taking is too dangerous: Black's best reply is 22…Ke8 23.Rxd7 Bxg5+ 24.f4 instead (the engine rates it +0.84).","Takes the pawn on d5.","Leaves Black with an isolated pawn on c6: a long-term weakness.","22.Rxd5 threatens Qd6+, winning a knight and a bishop, picking it up with 23.Qxd7+, and stops …Rxg5.","It threatens Qd6+, winning a knight and a bishop, picking it up with 23.Qxd7+, so Black has to spend the next move on it."],"why":[{"title":"The idea","text":"22.Rxd5!! offers the rook on d5. Taking it gives White the material back and more."},{"title":"What White gives up","text":"22.Rxd5 puts the rook on d5 where it can be taken by the c6 pawn. That's a whole rook on offer."},{"title":"If Black takes the rook","text":"22…cxd5 is met by 23.Nxd5+, taking the d5 pawn with check. Then 24.Nxf6 takes the bishop on f6, and 25.Qxg5 takes the rook on g5. White ends up two pawns ahead: White is winning (+5.14)."},{"title":"Black's best try","text":"Black's best is to leave the rook alone and play 22…Ke8. White answers 23.Rxd7, taking the knight on d7. Then 24.f4 threatens Rd3, winning a rook, and 25.fxg5 takes the bishop on g5. White is a pawn down: White is a little better (+0.84)."},{"title":"Without the sacrifice","text":"The best move without the sacrifice, 22.Bxf6+, is clearly weaker (−0.10 against +0.84). Black answers 22…Nxf6, taking the bishop on f6 and threatening …Rxg3, winning the queen for a rook. That would leave White level."}]},{"ply":45,"name":"23.Rxd7","cls":"brilliant","color":"w","headline":"23.Rxd7!! A real sacrifice: White gives up material and the engine still rates it best.","points":["Puts the rook on d7 where it can be taken.","Taking is too dangerous: Black's best reply is 23…Bxg5+ 24.f4 Kxd7 25.fxg5 instead (the engine rates it +0.78).","Takes the knight on d7.","The rook reaches the seventh rank, where 2 pawns sit and the king is cut off on the back rank.","23.Rxd7 trades off the attacked rook instead of losing it to …cxd5.","Black was threatening …cxd5, winning a rook for a pawn. The rook takes something with it instead."],"why":[{"title":"The idea","text":"23.Rxd7!! leaves the bishop on g5 hanging. Taking it gives White an attack worth more than the bishop."},{"title":"What White gives up","text":"23.Rxd7 leaves the bishop on g5 hanging to the bishop on f6 and the rook on g8. That's a bishop on offer."},{"title":"What it does instead","text":"It takes the knight on d7. Now Black can take only one of the two: the rook on d7 or the bishop on g5."},{"title":"If Black takes the rook","text":"23…Kxd7 is met by 24.Qd3+. Then 26.Rd1 threatens Bf4+, winning a bishop for a pawn, and 27.c3 attacks the bishop on d4. White is still two pawns down, but the attack is worth more: White is clearly better (+2.00)."},{"title":"If Black takes the bishop","text":"23…Bxg5+ is met by 24.f4, threatening Rd3, winning a rook and a pawn. Then 25.fxg5 takes the bishop on g5, and 26.Qd3+ gives check. White is two pawns down: White is a little better (+0.88). This is Black's best try."},{"title":"Without the sacrifice","text":"The best move without the sacrifice, 23.Rf5, is clearly weaker (−0.26 against +0.78). Black answers 23…h6, threatening …Rxg5, winning a bishop. That would leave White level."}]},{"ply":53,"name":"27.Nd6+","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"27.Nd6+! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["The knight forks the king and the pawn: both can't be saved at once.","Moving away uncovers the rook on e1, which now hits the e6 pawn.","The next best move, 27.Kb1, would drop White's winning chances from 72% to 53% (+0.32).","27.Nd6+ wins the exchange, picking it up with 28.Qxd6, and forks the king and the pawn.","Sets up a sequence and wins the exchange once the captures settle, picking it up with 28.Qxd6.","Black answers 27…Rxd6, taking the knight on d6."]},{"ply":87,"name":"44.g7","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"44.g7! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Pushes the passed pawn to g7, close to promotion.","The next best move, 44.a3, would drop White's winning chances from 90% to 58% (+0.89).","44.g7 pushes the passed pawn to g7.","Black answers 44…f2.","After 44…f2 45.g8=Q f1=Q 46.Qd5+ Kb6 47.Qd6+, the pawn promotes on g8 and the pawn promotes on f1 (+5.97)."]},{"ply":91,"name":"46.Qd5+","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"46.Qd5+! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["The queen forks the king and the pawn: both can't be saved at once.","The next best move, 46.Qh7+, would drop White's winning chances from 84% to 68% (+2.10).","46.Qd5+ forks the king and the pawn.","Black answers 46…Kb6.","After 46…Kb6 47.Qd6+ Kb7 48.Qxc5 Qf6+ 49.Qc3, White comes out a pawn up (+3.71)."]},{"ply":123,"name":"62.Qc4","cls":"miss","color":"w","headline":"62.Qc4 misses the chance 61…Qb5 gave: 62.Qg7+ would have punished it. White's winning chances go from 93% to 78%.","points":["Black answers 62…Qf5: activates the queen (from 11 to 21 usable squares).","Better was 62.Qg7+ (+7.08), which gives check, so the reply is forced."],"better":"62.Qg7+ gives check. Engine line: 62…Kb8 63.Qf8+ Kb7 64.Qe7+ Ka8 65.Qd8+ (+7.08)."}],"opening":{"name":"Rapport-Jobava System","eco":"D01","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 6…a6: 12 moves in all, 6 by White and 6 by Black.","Theory runs out after 6…a6: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}